WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:04.571
A loaded truck and a tennis ball are both coming at you at 20 metres per second.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:07.056
Which one would you rather stop with your hands?

00:00:07.056 --> 00:00:09.179
Two things make the truck harder to stop.

00:00:09.179 --> 00:00:10.930
Pause, and say what they are.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.532
Its mass, and how fast it's going.

00:00:15.532 --> 00:00:19.139
Today we turn 'hard to stop' into a number.

00:00:19.139 --> 00:00:21.150
It's called momentum.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.920
Learn this word for word.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.650
It comes straight from SAGS.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:32.040
Linear momentum is the product of the mass and velocity of the object.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:36.570
p equals m v.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:44.220
Kilograms times metres per second, so the unit is the kilogram metre per second.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.720
Same ball, same speed.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.370
One goes east, one goes west.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:51.900
Same momentum?

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:53.050
No.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.520
Momentum is a vector.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:01:01.180
With east positive, one is plus 6,24 and the other is minus 6,24.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.780
Same size, opposite signs.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.780
Keep that in mind, because the signs matter for the rest of this module.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:16.700
Cricket ball, 156 grams, 135 kilometres an hour, due west.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:20.020
First, I choose east as positive.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.700
Next I convert.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:30.300
156 grams divided by 1 000 is 0,156 kilograms.

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:39.330
135 divided by 3,6 is 37,5 metres per second, but it's going west,

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:42.350
so it's minus 37,5.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:46.310
Then p equals m v.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.570
Substitute, and I get minus 5,85.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:55.180
The answer is 5,85 kilogram metres per second, west.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.040
That's four marks.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:01.870
Watch where they come from: the conversion, the formula, the substitution,

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.640
and the answer with its direction.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:06.230
Pause.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.900
Why must the answer say west?

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.630
Because momentum is a vector.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.250
A number without a direction loses the mark.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:17.920
Your turn.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:25.950
Pause the video and do the cyclist on page 140: 65 kilograms,

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.720
8,5 metres per second north.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:35.930
552,5 kilogram metres per second, north.

00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:37.720
Did you remember north?

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:42.070
When a net force acts, the momentum changes.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.770
Change in momentum is final minus initial.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:49.840
Always final minus initial.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:54.630
Most marks are lost in two places.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:58.400
Step 2: say your positive direction.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:02.270
Step 3: give both velocities a sign.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:03.900
Predict.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.560
A ball hits a wall and stops.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:11.210
The same ball hits the wall and bounces back at the same speed.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.550
Which one has the bigger change in momentum?

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:16.670
Pause and decide.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.090
Look at the orange area.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.350
That's the change in momentum.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.690
Bouncing back makes it bigger.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:28.830
The ball has to stop, and then go the other way.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:33.920
Ball, 200 grams, comes in at 12 to the right.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:36.600
The bat sends it back at 8 to the left.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:43.800
Right is positive, so u is plus 12, and v is minus 8.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:49.090
Delta p is 0,2 times, minus 8 minus 12.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:55.030
That's 0,2 times minus 20, which is minus 4,00.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:04:09.570
So the change in momentum is 4,00 kilogram metres per second, to the left.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:18.640
A learner wrote 0,2 times, 8 minus 12, and got minus 0,80.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:19.930
Pause.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.360
What went wrong?

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.340
She dropped the minus sign on the 8.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.320
The velocity didn't change by 4.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.940
It went from plus 12 to minus 8.

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:31.740
That's a change of 20.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:33.660
Your turn.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.600
The soccer ball on page 143.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.600
East is positive.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.650
Pause and work it out.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:48.340
0,43 times, 14 minus minus 10.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.140
So 0,43 times 24.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:55.850
That's 10,32 kilogram metres per second, east.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:05:00.020
Newton's second law, in SAGS words.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:05.140
The net force acting on an object is equal to the rate of change of momentum.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:10.760
So F net equals delta p over delta t.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:14.370
Same ball, same bat.

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:18.650
It's in contact with the bat for 0,020 seconds.

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:24.430
Minus 4,00 divided by 0,020 is minus 200.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.530
So the force is 200 newtons, to the left.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:29.410
Pause.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.410
The ball was moving right.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:34.200
Why is the force on it to the left?

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:39.650
The force points the same way as the change in momentum.

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:42.170
It's the force that turns the ball around.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:46.990
Impulse is the product of the net force and the contact time.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:49.470
Impulse equals the change in momentum.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:56.200
Newton seconds and kilogram metres per second are the same unit.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:02.300
This orange rectangle is the impulse: force times time.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:08.140
Right now it's minus 2 newton seconds, with a force of minus 10 newtons.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:11.470
I'm going to make the stopping time four times longer.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.200
What happens to the force?

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.690
Pause and predict.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:19.460
The area stays the same, because it's the same stop.

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:22.920
The force drops to a quarter: 2,5 newtons.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:24.940
Keep this picture in mind.

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.460
It's the whole of the next part.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:31.410
Your turn: page 146.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:38.330
A 0,25 kilogram ball, 40 newtons to the left, for 0,015 seconds.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.850
Find the change in momentum, then the final velocity.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.260
Pause and work it out.

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:50.620
Minus 40 times 0,015 is minus 0,60.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:54.590
So 0,60 kilogram metres per second, to the left.

00:06:54.590 --> 00:07:04.510
Then v is 0,60 divided by 0,25, which is 2,40 metres per second, to the left.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.250
Same ball, same speed, same stop.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.780
So the same change in momentum.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:16.140
The only thing you can change is the time it takes to stop.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:20.050
This explanation is worth three marks in nearly every paper.

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:23.270
Say these three things, in this order.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:25.960
One: the change in momentum is the same.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:33.300
Two: the stopping time increases, and name what does it.

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:41.350
Three: F net is delta p over delta t, so the average force decreases.

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:47.130
Never say the airbag makes the change in momentum smaller.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:52.830
The November memo says it word for word: do not say that the change

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:55.240
in momentum becomes smaller.

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:56.850
Your turn.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:01.650
A goalkeeper pulls her hands back as she catches a hard shot.

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:04.930
Pause, and write the three-mark explanation.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:07.640
Same delta p.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:09.060
Longer stopping time.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:14.190
So a smaller average force.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:15.760
Three ticks.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:18.410
That's momentum and impulse.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:23.390
Next, in the app: Try it, the impulse lab on its own.

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:25.060
Then Practise.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.500
Then test yourself, with no help.
